#%PAM-1.0
# Proteus lock screen.
#
# Deliberately delegates to the distro stack instead of hand-rolling
# `auth required pam_unix.so`. Including system-auth means whatever the system
# already enforces — pam_faillock lockout, pam_faildelay, non-local accounts —
# applies at the lock screen too, rather than being silently bypassed.
#
# Install to /etc/pam.d/proteus-lock (see install/machine/install-lock-pam.sh).
# check-unlock.py falls back to the "login" service if this file is absent,
# so a missing install degrades to the previous behaviour rather than locking
# the user out.
auth      include   system-auth
account   include   system-auth
